  "description": "Aspiring inventors participate in a series of sprints to understand the invention process in IBM -- they learn and practice skills required to disclose an invention. ",
  "problemStatement": "As of 2017 only one Master Inventor is part of the MEA geography. There is a need to increase the number of inventors and inventions being generated from the MEA region; Unawareness or uncertainty about the IBM patenting process; missed opportunity for IBM",
  "outcome": "Aspiring inventors believing that they too can be an inventor -- a demystified patent process.   Aspiring inventors acquire skills required to disclose and submit an invention.  Expand the breadth and capabilities of an under-served market.  Increase the technical skills of IBMers in this developing market, allowing them to grow and develop their technical careers.  With the newly acquired skills, these new inventors will be able to expand the capability of IBM solutions by enhancing them to solve local challenges.",
  "finalOutcome": "Enhancing the technical eminence of more than 40 aspiring inventors in MEA.  Established a reference group to help lead to further development of inventors in MEA.",
